-- The database under ./db is autogenerated. Changing the entries there
-- will result in a data loss whenever a new database gets extracted.
-- To be able to customize and/or fix entries that aren't yet detected
-- by the extractor logic, this file here can be used to save overwrites.
--
-- This file was ported from questie-octo's Data/pfDB/overwrites-octo.lua.
-- It carries, in order:
--   1. records the Octo DB has that the TurtleWoW build does not
--   2. the Octo pack's own corrections
--   3. the TurtleWoW pack's own corrections
-- Records come first so that anything indexing into them further down finds
-- them present.
--
-- Port-specific changes vs. the questie-octo original:
--   * The "phantom zones" deletion block was REMOVED. pfQuest resolves zones
--     by numeric id, not by name, so the phantom 5000-series zone ids are
--     harmless here; questie-octo only needed them gone because its
--     GetMapIDByName walks the locale table with pairs().
--   * pfDB["octo-overwrites-complete"] was REMOVED (nothing in pfQuest reads it).

